# vehje. public API and composition

The framework's public crate: the two plug-in contracts (the grammar
contract on the input side, the target contract on the output side), the
re-exports a consumer builds against, the orchestration that runs a program
from grammar through the Core passes to a `Checked` residual, and the
distribution-composition entry point that links a set of targets at compile
time. A reference distribution lives here. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
